How to find your IP address?
1. Find Public IP (Internet Address)
• Google "What is my IP?"
2. Find Private IP (Local Network Address)
• Windows: ipconfig
• Linux/Mac: ifconfig or ip a

🧠 How IP address works?
1. Assigning an IP Address:
•When your device connects to the internet (via Wi-Fi, mobile data, or Ethernet):
•It is assigned an IP address by a router or an ISP (Internet Service Provider).
•This can be dynamic (changes over time) or static (permanently assigned).
2. Sending Data Using IP:
When you open a website:
•Your device sends a request packet to the server.
🎈 When data travels over the internet, it is divided into smaller units called Packets. These are like little envelopes containing the data and information needed for delivery.
•The packet includes:
👉 Your IP address (source)
👉 The server’s IP address (destination)
Routers along the way use the destination IP to forward the packet.
3. Receiving Response:
•The server sends a response back to your IP address.
•Your device knows to expect it because the request originated from your IP.

📘 Example:
•You type www.google.com.
•DNS translates it to IP 142.250.182.132.
•Your computer sends a request to that IP.
•Google’s server sees your IP and sends the page back to you.
